MLX builds of chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v4 (text only). Modifications relative to Qwen3.5-2B:
- all language-model weights were fine-tuned (full fine-tuning, bf16 training, two runs with different seeds whose
  final weights were averaged uniformly) to score typed decision questions (choice / score / true-false) with a
  verdict readout: logit(" yes") - logit(" no") at one " ->" slot per option, using the v2 input protocol (render v2
  with long-option catalogues; block-causal attention in the full-attention layers over 2,048-token blocks);
  calibration temperatures per question type were fitted afterwards (readout_config.json);
- these files hold the language model only: the vision tower (frozen during training) and the multi-token-prediction
  head are not included; the language-model tensors of chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v4 (revision
  3f2c063f7d94cfa281b9fee87a5b89bed6745506) were saved unchanged as a text-only Qwen3_5ForCausalLM with tied
  input/output embeddings (tensor names model.language_model.* -> model.*) and then converted;
- converted to MLX format with mlx-lm 0.31.3 / mlx 0.32.2 (https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm, MIT License,
  Copyright Apple Inc.): bf16/ = bfloat16, 8bit/ = affine 8-bit quantisation, group size 64; each folder also holds
  macjev_norms_fp32.safetensors (the exact FP32 (1 + w) RMSNorm weights);
- the runtime script contains a modified copy of mlx-lm 0.31.3's qwen3_5 GatedDeltaNet.__call__ (MIT License,
  Copyright Apple Inc.; the q/k normalisation epsilon changed and the sharding branches removed); the MIT copyright
  and permission notice is reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md;
- added the runtime script (jev_style_decision_mlx.py), readout/release configuration files, validation records,
  the integrity manifest and this NOTICE.

Training labels: soft labels for part of the training rows were distilled from TypeSafe Jev 1.14 via its public
API (/v1/systemone). No Jev weights or code are included. The other labels come from the public datasets and
generators listed in the main model card
(chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v4).

The question types (choice / score / noul) follow the typed-decision convention of Laya
(https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya, Apache-2.0) so both models can be evaluated on the same inputs. No Laya
code or weights are included.

Part of the Jev-Style decision series: v1 = chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-Qwen3.5-2B-Decision, v2 =
chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-Qwen3.5-2B-Decision-v2, v3 = chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-2B-Decision-v3 and
chaoliangUNSW/Jev-Style-0.8B-Decision-v3. This model was fine-tuned from Qwen/Qwen3.5-2B; no weights of the earlier
models were used (the v3 training rows were reused as part of the training data).

